														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1377271">
									

<p>Nice writing, good story. I upvoted, but I have one problem. Early on it says that Margaret has &quot;unbreakable skin&quot;, yet near the end she feels a syringe slip into the back of her neck-how did it penetrate? Also, it should at least be the cold sting of a needle-syringes hold the medication. (I won't even get into how hard it is to inject anything into the neck without paralyzing someone or damaging the blood vessels, etc. Just a personal peeve of mine for many years.)</p>

