														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1377341">
									

<p>In my headcannon for this story, Margret went on to become to become the protagonist in a superhero reconstruction story where she fights crime both mundane and paranormal while evading the foundation (who are just trying to do their jobs), and the major theme of the story is that individuals can make a difference even in a cold, uncaring universe. And SCP-353 becomes her arch nemesis, 732 acts as her (somewhat unhinged) voice with an internet connection that asks her to do all sorts of pointless arbitrary things but is sometimes helpful, <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">and Able is her boyfriend</span> okay no that wouldn't work.</p>
<p>The only reason I'm hesitant to actually write this is because it would be a very out-of-genre experience, and very easy to bring Margret into Mary Sue territory. Still, I'm certain that in the hands of a pro it could be a great story.</p>

							</div>

								
