					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/scratskinner" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(182900); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=182900&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608349698" alt="scratskinner" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=182900)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/scratskinner" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(182900); return false;" >scratskinner</a></span> <span class="odate time_1329646552 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">19 Feb 2012 10:15</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1377395">
									

<p>The story is okay. The portrayal of SCP-732&#8230;This is not SCP-732.<br />
SCP-732 looks like this (at least during Fanficization):<br />
<em>containm@#$@relevantcliche@#$@$#ecords</em><br />
not this:<br />
<em>Im 0mn1pR3s3nt t3xtu@l L0Lsp3@k3R</em><br />
It bugs me to no end that people keep thinking &quot;Fanfic Plague&quot; means &quot;Leetspeak Entity&quot;.</p>
<p>Also, there is no indication that SCP-732 can spontaneously appear where there is no pre-existing writing. And&#8230; &quot;SCP-732 is a force <strong>or</strong> entity&#8230;&quot; Note the &quot;or&quot;. There is a fine line that SCP-732 sits on. I call it &quot;plausible deniability of self-awareness&quot;. You cannot have a conversation with SCP-732, for that would show it to be an entity, and not a force.</p>
<p>On a more constructive note, I suggest changing the conversation with &quot;732&quot; to a straightforward diary entry carved into the wall (or written on regular paper, there <em>is</em> a desk mentioned), featuring her worries about the creepy Dr. Husmann and her general situation. Then the trying to sleep. Wakes up to find it reworked into a romance wherein &quot;Margaret&quot; is rescued from &quot;Husmann&quot;. About everything else stays the same.</p>
<p>Alternately, this is 732-spawned (from accidental crosstesting) and not 732 proper.</p>
<p>How does that sound to you?</p>

							</div>

								
