					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/eskobar" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1173523); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1173523&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608349698" alt="Eskobar" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1173523)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/eskobar" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1173523); return false;" >Eskobar</a></span> <span class="odate time_1329663308 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">19 Feb 2012 14:55</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1377496">
									

<p>Hmm. The part about writing and editing the diary entry falls into the territory of &quot;wish I had thought of that before.&quot;</p>
<p>I do appreciate the criticism, being the author of the relevant article. On that note, I really, really had no idea you were still around at all, or I would have run the idea by you before using the SCP. That's my bad, sorry.</p>
<p>Regarding the changes, though, there are particular reasons for 732's behavior, mostly centered around my headcanon regarding 732's ability. The sparse amount of detail regarding 732, which is specifically why I always loved the article so much, allows for a great deal of interpretation in one's personal depiction of the character, <em>especially</em> if you take the Clef-Kondraki war to be canon. There, 732 is far more powerful, and its range and writing style are far more fluid. My version makes him an impotent god, able to flit around and change information at will, but not able to do anything to anyone in person. The writing style is partially designed because I thought it was foreign enough to be recognizable as 732, but familiar enough to someone like Margaret to be more comforting than its usual abject insane screaming.</p>
<p>Generally speaking, if you like, there's nothing in particular saying outright that the entity being spoken with <strong>is</strong> 732 and not an alternate/offspring version of 732, so there's wiggle room for everybody's headcanon. In fact, if you consider that the head of RAISA is aware of increased 732 activity (via email) and still has no idea that her email is tampered with, there's additional evidence that this might be something else entirely.</p>

							</div>

								
					
