			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1476468">
									

<p>Well&#8230; I should imagine that - if the community liked it - it would be upvoted and - even if reluctantly - accepted, or changed at the decision of the author. Otherwise it would be downvoted and deleted (which is the probable outcome).</p>
<p>I might add that your example is <em>blatantly</em> inconsistent with it's given article: I agree with you on that point. SCP-732, however, is written vaguely enough to allow for such interpretations, regardless of your intent. SCP-732 is one of the few exceptions which would allow (given the whole 'meta' thing) for this, which makes your example a little incompatable.</p>
<p>As stated above, this doesn't necesarily have to be considered an effect of SCP-732. Death of the Author applies here as well. It reads just as well without that aspect.</p>

							</div>

								
