														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1476536">
									

<p>And I might point out you have no way of proving whether or not it is <em>communicating</em>, which is what that &quot;force or entity&quot; is there for. Really, unfalsifiabilty aside, if something's red in the original, and blue in the story based on it, you need to account for why it is now blue. See XYZ in my last post.</p>
<p>If you like it because it corrupts its own containment, perhaps you should reread the containment procedures. Particularly the &quot;currently uncont&quot; and the &quot;if containable&quot; bits. And &quot;I can do X, you can do Y, there ain't a problem to solve&quot; seems a bit patronizing. As for the story being clear of 732 involvement, there's that &quot;increased activity from 732&quot; bit. And you pretty clearly intended it to be 732, given your comments on this page.</p>

