														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1476579">
									

<p>SCP-732 is <em>depicted</em> as being blue, to use your analogy, in an article centered on the basic ability of SCP-732 to render documentation unreliable at will. Meaning there is at least leeway present to interpret it as red. Though I think that analogy stretches the difference we're talking about here; you have an incorporeal something-or-other that has been observed communicating through fan-fic dialogue, I have an incorporeal something-or-other that is observed communicating through leetspeak. It's not exactly apples and oranges.</p>
<p>I'm aware it's not <em>actually</em> contained; you know what I mean. It is capable of altering documentation pertaining to its existence, making almost any reasonable interpretation of its abilities/characteristics viable. We disagree about what constitutes &quot;reasonable interpretation&quot;; I'm satisfied with what I've written, you're not. That's not patronizing, that's an accurate description of reality at this moment.</p>
<p>With regards to the is-it-732 matter: yes, I intended the unnamed entity responsible for the plot to be my headcanonical interpretation of SCP-732. But the parts of the article regarding the primary plot have no reference to the article by name; the number is referenced in passing, with no indication of a connection between Maria Jones' messages and the events of the story. But just to eliminate that much possible overlap, I changed the 732 reference. Again, I'm satisfied with what I've done, and don't intend to make further alterations at present.</p>

							</div>

								
