			<div class="content" id="post-content-1477046">
									

<p>The reply button didn't show up on lycan's post, which is why I've replied to Theally's.</p>
<p>@lycan: The first three boil down to &quot;a <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">wizard</span> reality bender did it&quot;. A hallucination wouldn't have got 2122 out of the cell and Husmann into it.</p>
<p>Crosstest - unless you can show which particular SCPs would produce this result, it's a cop-out. Non-mainlist SCP - Unless it's explicitly mentioned that this is an SCP unknown to the general readership, this is a cop-out.</p>
<p>Tell me, upon reading this story, was the first thing to come to mind about the leetspeaking entity that &quot;It's a reality bender&quot;? or &quot;It's a hallucination&quot;? or &quot;it's a cross-test&quot; or &quot;it's something we haven't heard of?&quot; Are these conclusions the story naturally leads you to?</p>
<p>The idea here is to find something that fits more criteria for being this entity than 732 does. The idea here is to find something such that people's first impressions will be &quot;oh hey, it must be this&quot; rather than &quot;oh hey, it must be 732&quot;.</p>
<p>@Theally: doesn't fit Fred's modus operandi. He's a cameo, and it's quite a leap from &quot;hears about 4chan&quot; to &quot;speaks exclusively in 4chanish&quot;.</p>

