			<div class="content" id="post-content-1477149">
									

<p>@Lycan:So your answer to crosstest is: Basically 732. But up to 11. Or his twin brother. And Fred is there, too. Known to be fluent in leetspeak, is Fred.</p>
<p>Also, from SCP-423's article: &quot;It cannot enter electronic storage, or affect purely visual narratives.&quot; Clearly responsible for framing Husmann, is this Fred.</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Bitter Serpent's Hand member, all well and good, <em>but it's not in the story</em>. No hints in the text that the Serpent's Hand has anything to do with this.</span></p>
<p>If you're talking about &quot;110-Montauk has nothing to with rape&quot;, I'd like to point out the discussion over there indicates that, heck yes, it does matter. The most obvious conclusion will be the most <em>remembered</em> conclusion, and the most downvoted/upvoted for. There isn't any guarantee that someone's going to see the discussion thread about how X is not actually X and why you're so silly for thinking it could ever be X. Let alone agree with it. (I am aware of the irony.)</p>
<p>Alone does not mean wrong. And I'd like to point out that as the author of SCP-732, I have a vested interest in ensuring 732 is portrayed in the least inaccurate way possible, and/or that something else is not mistaken for same.</p>
<p>@Eskobar, should he be reading this, my main quibble (at the moment) with 732 being this entity is that it's leetspeaking for no good reason. If you have a good reason lurking in your headcanon, to account for the difference between 732-in-article and 732-in-story, working it in may help. At the very least, why isn't 2122 asking &quot;Hey, why are you talking funny?&quot; A more minor quibble is the carving in walls, which could be fixed by removing the references to blank wall.</p>
<p>@Theally: From the story: &quot;This was different, though, because she had been here almost a full day, and she was almost certain that this wall had been blank. Sterile, cold, and perfectly blank.&quot;</p>

