<p>May want to split this thread off since it's nested too deeply, but I digress.</p>
<p>I think I understand where scrat is coming from. I would guess that SCP-732 speaking in leet<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-971774-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-971774-1')">1</a></sup> is as grating to scratskinner as people attributing SCP-804 to AWCY? was to Sorts.</p>
<p>Well, okay, maybe only half as grating, but really the leet doesn't add anything extra. Replace the leet with normal text and the article reads exactly the same.</p>
<p>On the other hand, replace the leet with fragments that you found on some fan-fiction sites and maybe that's another experience altogether and adds even more weird to the story.</p>
<p>Edit: And don't get me wrong, it's not a bad story by any means.</p>
